.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.gage" "kobas.gage"
.SH NAME
kobas.gage \- GAGE style gene set enrichment analysis (KOBAS SNBEA)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.gage(\fBexpr\fR as any, 
\fBcls\fR as any, 
\fBgmt\fR as any, 
\fBmin_size\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBmax_size\fR as integer = 500, 
\fBfdr\fR as string = "BH", 
\fBdata_type\fR as string = "rseq", 
\fBnormalize\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
GAGE style gene set enrichment analysis (KOBAS SNBEA)
 
 Aggregate the gene level t statistics of each gene set into a gene set level
 z-score (\fBsum(t) / sqrt(n)\fR) and estimate the significance from the upper tail
 of the standard normal distribution.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBexpr\fB \fR\- the expression matrix (matrix object, \fBdataframe\fR or expression matrix file path).. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcls\fB \fR\- the phenotype class labels, same as the \fBcls\fR parameter of \fBkobas.gsea\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgmt\fB \fR\- the gene set collection: a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model or a GMT file path.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_size\fB \fR\- the minimum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB5\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_size\fB \fR\- the maximum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB500\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfdr\fB \fR\- the multiple testing correction method, default \fBBH\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdata_type\fB \fR\- the data type of the expression matrix: \fBrseq\fR (default) or \fBma\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnormalize\fB \fR\- performs the data normalization before the analysis? Default \fBTRUE\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR with the gene set id as the row names and the columns: \fBname\fR,
 \fBdescription\fR, \fBsize\fR, \fBstatistic\fR, \fBpvalue\fR, \fBp_adjust\fR and \fBgenes\fR.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The returned p-value is the upper tail probability, that means the gene set is
 enriched in the second phenotype group (the samples labeled with \fB1\fR).
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
